-- title:
--   Edge charts covering a formal Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ is a prime number.
--
--   **Base data.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (hypothesis `hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal O/\pi$ has exactly $r$ elements, and $r$ and $\pi$ generate the same ideal of $\mathcal O$ (absolute unramifiedness); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficient ring.** $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and an $\mathcal O$-algebra, $\mathrm{Fr}$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of it, and four hypotheses are imposed: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a group homomorphism subject to `hvdet`: $v\!\det(g) = n$ holds precisely when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Group data.** $G$ is a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ are homomorphisms with $\rho$ the composite of $\sigma$ with the projection (`hρ`), and $\Gamma \le G$ is a subgroup containing an element whose image under $\sigma$ is a scalar matrix and has $v\!\det$ equal to $2$ (`hcent`) and an element with $v\!\det$ equal to $1$ (`hodd`). The subgroup $\Gamma' \le G$ consists exactly of the elements of $\Gamma$ with even $v\!\det \circ \sigma$ (`hΓ'`). On the vertices of the Bruhat–Tits tree — homothety classes of full lattices in $K_0^2$, i.e. [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) — the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ has finite vertex stabilisers (`hdisc`) and finitely many orbits, witnessed by a finite set of vertices meeting every orbit (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The scheme.** $\mathcal X$ is a scheme and $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ is proper and flat.
--
--   **The quotient map.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\Theta$ assigns to each pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (a `DeligneDatum` for $\pi$ over $K_0$: an assignment $M \mapsto$ a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$, for $M$ running over full lattices of $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, monotone under inclusions of lattices, equivariant for scalar homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$) a $B$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathcal X$ whose composite with $f$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathcal O \to B$. Four hypotheses govern $\Theta$: naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hΘnat`); invariance under the twisted action of $\Gamma$ (`hΘinv`), where `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ relates $(\psi, d)$ to $(\psi', d')$ when $\psi' = \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det(g)}$ and $d'$ is the pullback of $d$ along $g^{-1}$, i.e. $d'(M)$ is the preimage of $d(g^{-1}M)$ under the base-changed lattice isomorphism for every full lattice $M$; the fibre description (`hΘfib`) over algebraically closed $\mathcal O$-fields $k$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, asserting for each fixed $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ that every $k$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ is $\Theta(\psi, P)$ for some Deligne datum $P$, and that $\Theta(\psi,P) = \Theta(\psi,P')$ holds exactly when $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ are related by the twisted action of some $\gamma \in \Gamma$; and the categorical quotient property (`hΘuniv`): for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every assignment $\rho'$ of $B$-points of $T$ to the same input data which is natural and twisted-$\Gamma$-invariant, there is a family $u$ of maps from $B$-points of $\mathcal X$ to $B$-points of $T$, natural in $B$, with $u \circ \Theta = \rho'$, and any other natural family with this property agrees with $u$ pointwise.
--
--   **Chart matrix and thickenings.** $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi, 1)$. For each $n$, $s_n$ is the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1}) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ induced by the structure map (`hsn`), $t_n$ is the closed immersion $\operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1}) \to \operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+2})$ induced by the quotient factorisation (`htn`), and $t_n$ followed by $s_{n+1}$ equals $s_n$ (`htsn`). Writing $X_n$ for the fibre product of $f$ and $s_n$, the morphisms $j_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$ are compatible with both projections: $j_n$ followed by the first projection is the first projection (`hjn₁`), and $j_n$ followed by the second projection equals the second projection followed by $t_n$ (`hjn₂`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $A$ denote `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r`, by definition the localisation away from the element `edgeQuot.discr` of the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ by the principal ideal generated by `edgeRel`, with its two distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η`; and let $A_n := A/(\pi^{n+1})$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the $(n+1)$-st power of the image of $\pi$. Then there exist
--
--   - for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $n \in \mathbb N$ an open subset $U_{h,n}$ of $X_n$,
--
--   - a ring homomorphism $c_{h,n}$ from the sections of the structure sheaf of $X_n$ over $U_{h,n}$ to $A_n$,
--
--   - a morphism $\kappa_{h,n} : \operatorname{Spec} A_n \to X_n$,
--
--   satisfying the following six conditions.
--
--   (i) For all $h$ and $n$, the preimage $\kappa_{h,n}^{-1}(U_{h,n})$ is all of $\operatorname{Spec} A_n$, and for every section $s$ over $U_{h,n}$ the element $c_{h,n}(s)$ is the element of $A_n$ corresponding, under `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, to the restriction to the whole space of the pullback $\kappa_{h,n}^{*}(s)$; thus $c_{h,n}$ is restriction of functions along the chart morphism.
--
--   (ii) For all $h$, $n$ and every $y \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$: applying $c_{h,n}$ to the section over $U_{h,n}$ obtained by taking the global section of $\operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$ given by $y \bmod \pi^{n+1}$, pulling it back along the second projection $X_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$ and restricting to $U_{h,n}$, yields the class in $A_n$ of the image of $y$ in $A$.
--
--   (iii) For all $h$ and $n$: $U_{h,n} = j_n^{-1}(U_{h,n+1})$, and for every section $s$ over $U_{h,n+1}$ the value $c_{h,n}$ on the restriction of $j_n^{*}(s)$ equals the reduction of $c_{h,n+1}(s)$ under the natural surjection $A_{n+1} \to A_n$.
--
--   (iv) For all $h$, $n$, every commutative ring $B$ which is both an $\mathcal O$-algebra and an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra compatibly, with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, every $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra map $\bar x : A_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, P$ over $B$: if $d$ is the chart datum attached to $\bar x$, meaning that $d$ assigns to the standard full lattice $M_0$ the $B$-span of $\bar x(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, assigns to $g_1 M_0$ the image under the base-changed action of $g_1$ of the $B$-span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar x(\eta) \otimes e_1$ (here $\xi, \eta$ are taken modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ and $e_0, e_1$ is the standard basis), and $d$ satisfies `DeligneDatum.InEdgeChart` for the pair $(g_1M_0, M_0)$, that is, the edge non-degeneracy conditions at every prime ideal of $B$; and if $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$, then the morphism underlying $\Theta_B$ applied to the pair consisting of the structural map $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and $P$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\bar x)$ followed by $\kappa_{h,n}$ followed by the first projection $X_n \to \mathcal X$.
--
--   (v) For every $n$, the supremum of the open sets $U_{h,n}$ over all $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is the whole of $X_n$: the charts cover each thickening.
--
--   (vi) For every $h$, two statements hold. First, faithfulness: if $s$ and $s'$ are two systems of sections, $s_m$ and $s'_m$ over $U_{h,m}$, each compatible with the transition maps (the restriction of $j_m^{*}(s_{m+1})$ is $s_m$, and likewise for $s'$), and $c_{h,m}(s_m) = c_{h,m}(s'_m)$ for all $m$, then $s = s'$. Second, for every family $(\mathrm{fam}_m)_m$ with $\mathrm{fam}_m \in A_m$ compatible under the reductions $A_{m+1} \to A_m$, the existence of a compatible system $s$ of sections over the $U_{h,m}$ with $c_{h,m}(s_m) = \mathrm{fam}_m$ for all $m$ is equivalent to the following invariance condition: for every $m$, every ring $B$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra compatibly with $\pi$ nilpotent, every pair of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra maps $\bar x, \bar x' : A_m \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, d', P, P'$ over $B$ such that $d$ is the chart datum attached to $\bar x$ and $d'$ the chart datum attached to $\bar x'$ in the sense of (iv) (prescribed lines at $M_0$ and at $g_1M_0$, and lying in the edge chart for $(g_1M_0, M_0)$), such that $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$ and $P'$ the pullback of $d'$ along $h^{-1}$, and such that $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma'$, one has $\bar x(\mathrm{fam}_m) = \bar x'(\mathrm{fam}_m)$.
--
--   This is the chart description of the formal completion along the special fibre of a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient: the $\pi$-adic thickenings $X_n$ of $\mathcal X$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ are covered by the standard edge charts of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane, the chart morphisms are compatible with the thickening maps and with the coefficient ring, they are computed by $\Theta$ on chart Deligne data, and the functions on a chart are exactly the $\Gamma'$-invariant elements of the chart ring in the stated pointwise sense. It is obtained from the existence of a formal quotient datum and the comparison isomorphism for the quotient, and is used in the identification of holomorphic functions on the generic fibre in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient).
